## PR Title
Cleanup memory instructions and swap assert_equals parameters

## PR Description
The contributor notes the scope may have grown beyond the original assignment but believes the changes are an improvement. Three main modifications:

1. Reorders `assert_equals` parameters to match actual usage patterns observed in the codebase, keeping each assertion on a single line so error message line numbers remain accurate.
2. Simplifies the MemoryLoad module by collapsing the separate code paths for signed and unsigned memory loads, potentially helping the compiler optimize better.
3. Adds comprehensive test coverage for memory-load operations, addressing gaps in existing tests (including RISCOF) that had failed to catch issues such as "16-to-32-bit sign extension using the wrong bits."

The contributor acknowledges the new tests are extensive and unpolished, and notes that store-operation testing would be a useful follow-up.

